markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Jobs of Data

Professional apps don't just use live data—they also use **local** data for two important purposes.



APIs are powerful, but they are also fragile. A server might go down, or a user’s Wi-Fi might dro. **Backup data** is our “safety net” that keeps the app functional even when things go wrong.


<!-- TWO SIDE-BY-SIDE DIV BOXES -->
<div style="width:90%; margin:30px auto; text-align:center;">

<!-- CARD 1 -->
<div style="display:inline-block; vertical-align:top; width:360px; margin:20px 15px; background-color:#ffffff; color:#000000; padding:20px; border-radius:10px; box-shadow:2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); text-align:left;">
<p style="font-size:14pt; font-weight:bold; margin:0 0 10px 0; text-align:center;">Job 1: Static Constants</p>

<!-- Optional image (use if you upload/crop the left half) -->
<!-- <img src="PASTE_LEFT_CARD_IMAGE_URL_HERE" alt="Job 1: Static Constants" style="width:100%; height:140px; object-fit:cover; border-radius:8px; margin-bottom:12px;"> -->

<ul style="font-size:12pt; line-height:1.25; margin:0; padding-left:22px;">
      <li>Defines the app’s structure (name, labels, layout)</li>
      <li>Renders the UI instantly</li>
      <li><strong>Example:</strong> The app title or navigation menu text</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <!-- CARD 2 -->
<div style="display:inline-block; vertical-align:top; width:360px; margin:20px 15px; background-color:#ffffff; color:#000000; padding:20px; border-radius:10px; box-shadow:2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); text-align:left;">
<p style="font-size:14pt; font-weight:bold; margin:0 0 10px 0; text-align:center;">Job 2: Backup Data</p>

<!-- Optional image (use if you upload/crop the right half) -->
<!-- <img src="PASTE_RIGHT_CARD_IMAGE_URL_HERE" alt="Job 2: Backup Data" style="width:100%; height:140px; object-fit:cover; border-radius:8px; margin-bottom:12px;"> -->

<ul style="font-size:12pt; line-height:1.25; margin:0; padding-left:22px;">
      <li>Matches the API response</li>
      <li>Used if live data fails to load</li>
      <li><strong>Example:</strong> Sample list shown when the API is offline</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

</div>

<!-- TEACHER TIP BOX -->
<div style="background-color: #e4e2f8; border-radius: 10px; color: #000000; width: 95%; padding: 1px 20px 1px 20px; margin: 10px auto;">
  <p style="line-height: 1.5; margin: 10px; font-size: 12pt;">
    <b> 💡 Teaching Tip: </b>
    Emphasize that backup data must have the <strong>exact same structure</strong> (the same keys like <code>title</code> or <code>image</code>) as the real API data.
    If they don’t match, the code will break when it switches to the backup.
  </p>
</div>

## Up Next 
You will create an <strong>app shell</strong> so the screen is not blank while waiting for an API.

MARKDOWN
